Thanks for working on this!

One detail regarding `gen_ai.output.messages`: in the Responses API ([API reference](https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/responses/object)), a single model response returns a flat `output` list containing all generated items (reasoning, message/text, and tool calls). For example, when the model generates assistant text and multiple tool calls:

```json
{
  "output": [
    {
      "type": "message",
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": [{"type": "output_text", "text": "I will check the weather for both cities."}]
    },
    {
      "type": "function_call",
      "call_id": "call_1",
      "name": "get_weather",
      "arguments": "{\"location\": \"Seattle, WA\"}"
    },
    {
      "type": "function_call",
      "call_id": "call_2",
      "name": "get_weather",
      "arguments": "{\"location\": \"Boston, MA\"}"
    }
  ]
}
```

In OpenTelemetry GenAI semconv, `gen_ai.output.messages` represents candidate/choice completions generated by the model. Since all these items are produced in a single generation, they should be mapped as parts of a single assistant message:

```json
[
  {
    "role": "assistant",
    "parts": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "I will check the weather for both cities."
      },
      {
        "type": "tool_call",
        "id": "call_1",
        "name": "get_weather",
        "arguments": {"location": "Seattle, WA"}
      },
      {
        "type": "tool_call",
        "id": "call_2",
        "name": "get_weather",
        "arguments": {"location": "Boston, MA"}
      }
    ],
    "finish_reason": "tool_call"
  }
]
```

So what we did for putput messages was right (well aligned with what OpenAI thinks about it).

I see how it's asymmetrical with input messages and that we're forcing out input messages model onto openai Responses API where tool call requests are not messages per se.

In chat completions, each tool call request was individual message with unique tool call id, so the choice here is to stay consistent across openai flavors for input messages.
